Description: hold a pull request with no checks for 60 seconds on the same head before it is ready
Author: Azhou AI Hub
Forwarded: no

A repository that configures no check at all and the seconds after a push,
before GitHub registers the new head's checks, are the same reading: the fast
path and the GraphQL rollup both report nothing. The watcher treated that as a
clean head and reported the pull request ready to merge while its CI had not
registered yet, so a workflow that failed a moment later was never seen. A head
must keep reporting no checks for NO_CHECKS_CONFIRM_SECONDS before the pull
request is ready, and a push restarts that window.

